the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base annuity_withdrawal includes these resources:
    temporal.

the functions are:
    the gross amount of *an activity* is *an amount*.
    the effective date of *an activity* is *a date*.
    the account value of the policy before *an activity* is *an amount*.
    the issue date of the policy before *an activity* is *a date*.
    the duration of *an activity* is *a number*.
    the policy year of *an activity* is *a number*.
    the free amount of *an activity* is *an amount*.
    the excess of *an activity* is *an amount*.
    the chargeable amount of *an activity* is *an amount*.
    the surrender charge rate of *an activity* is *a number*.
    the surrender charge of *an activity* is *an amount*.
    the net amount of *an activity* is *an amount*.
    the remaining value of *an activity* is *an amount*.
    the free withdrawal percent of the plan is *a number*.
    the minimum balance of the plan is *an amount*.
    the account value of the policy after *an activity* is *a value*.

the templates are:
    *an activity* is a withdrawal.
    *an activity* fails the check *a code*.
    *an activity* spawns *a transaction*.
    the surrender charge rate for duration *a duration* is *a rate* under table surrender_charge.

the table surrender_charge is loaded from surrender_charge.csv, with unique match:
    duration | rate

the knowledge base annuity_withdrawal includes:

the text of "Withdrawal/Transaction.xml" is at "sources/Withdrawal/Transaction.xml".

the free withdrawal percent of the plan is 10, as stated in "PlanFields.csv" at FreeWithdrawalPercent.

the minimum balance of the plan is 2000, as stated in "PlanFields.csv" at MinimumBalance.

% An activity of this program is a withdrawal: the Withdrawal transaction it processes.
an activity is a withdrawal if
    the effective date of the activity is a date.

rule duration with provenance "Withdrawal/Transaction.xml" at MathVariable DurationMV:
the duration of an activity is a number if
    the age on the effective date of the activity of someone born on the issue date of the policy before the activity is the number.

rule policy_year with provenance "Withdrawal/Transaction.xml" at MathVariable PolicyYearMV:
the policy year of an activity is a number N if
    the duration of the activity is a number M
    and N = M + 1.

rule free_amount with provenance "Withdrawal/Transaction.xml" at MathVariable FreeAmountMV:
the free amount of an activity is an amount N if
    the account value of the policy before the activity is an amount M
    and the free withdrawal percent of the plan is a number K
    and N = round(M * K / 100 * 100) / 100.

rule excess with provenance "Withdrawal/Transaction.xml" at MathVariable ExcessMV:
the excess of an activity is an amount N if
    the gross amount of the activity is an amount M
    and the free amount of the activity is an amount K
    and N = M - K.

rule chargeable_amount with provenance "Withdrawal/Transaction.xml" at MathVariable ChargeableAmountMV:
the chargeable amount of an activity is an amount N if
    the gross amount of the activity is an amount M
    and the free amount of the activity is an amount K
    and M > K
    and the excess of the activity is N
    otherwise the activity is a withdrawal
    and N = 0.

rule surrender_charge_rate with provenance "Withdrawal/Transaction.xml" at MathVariable SurrenderChargeRateMV:
the surrender charge rate of an activity is a number N if
    the policy year of the activity is a second number
    and the surrender charge rate for duration the second number is N under table surrender_charge
    otherwise the activity is a withdrawal
    and N = 0.

rule surrender_charge with provenance "Withdrawal/Transaction.xml" at MathVariable SurrenderChargeMV:
the surrender charge of an activity is an amount N if
    the policy year of the activity is a number M
    and M > 7
    and N = 0
    otherwise the chargeable amount of the activity is an amount K
    and the surrender charge rate of the activity is a number P
    and N = round(K * P * 100) / 100.

rule net_amount with provenance "Withdrawal/Transaction.xml" at MathVariable NetAmountMV:
the net amount of an activity is an amount N if
    the gross amount of the activity is an amount M
    and the surrender charge of the activity is an amount K
    and N = round((M - K) * 100) / 100.

rule remaining_value with provenance "Withdrawal/Transaction.xml" at MathVariable RemainingValueMV:
the remaining value of an activity is an amount N if
    the account value of the policy before the activity is an amount M
    and the gross amount of the activity is an amount K
    and N = round((M - K) * 100) / 100.

% The withdrawal must be a positive amount.
rule w001 with provenance "Withdrawal/ValidateExpressions.xml" at Expression W001:
an activity fails the check "W001" if
    the gross amount of the activity <= 0.

% A withdrawal of [the gross amount] exceeds the account value of [the account value].
rule w002 with provenance "Withdrawal/ValidateExpressions.xml" at Expression W002:
an activity fails the check "W002" if
    the gross amount of the activity > the account value of the policy before the activity.

rule spawn_1 with provenance "Withdrawal/SpawnActivities.xml" at Spawn 1:
an activity spawns FullSurrender if
    the remaining value of the activity is an amount N
    and the minimum balance of the plan is an amount M
    and N < M
        and N > 0
    and it is not the case that the activity fails the check a code.

rule copy_account_value with provenance "Withdrawal/CopyToPolicyFields.xml" at Field AccountValue:
the account value of the policy after an activity is a value if
    the remaining value of the activity is the value
    and it is not the case that the activity fails the check a code.

